<title>USA: Barclays, WPP among Julian Robertson picks - Barron's.</title>
<headline>Barclays, WPP among Julian Robertson picks - Barron's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tiger Management's Julian Robertson's picks include airlines and banking companies, such as Barclays Plc and Citicorp, Barron's reported Sunday.</p>
<p>Barron's said Robertson, whose company manages about $8 billion in assets in its hedge funds, favors AMR and believes the parent of American Airlines stands to make the biggest gains from industry trends.</p>
<p>Robertson believes USAir Group Inc could add between $2 and $4 a share in earnings from a labor settlement with its pilots and earn $7 a share in two or three years, according to an interview in Barron's.</p>
<p>Besides Citicorp and Barclays, Robertson also named Wells Fargo as a favorite, the financial weekly reported.</p>
<p>Barron's said Robertson praised Tosco Corp, advertising conglomerate WPP Group and owns Morgan Stanley, Intel and Uni Storebrand of Norway.</p>
<p>Robertson is short on Japanese retailer Daiei Inc and Grupo Tribasa, the Mexican construction company, Barron's said.</p>
</text>
